 ```
 
 No API key or authorization JSON belongs in the repository.
+
+## Alerts and external monitoring
+
+1. Set a channel in `/etc/aurora/aurora.env`: `AURORA_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` + `AURORA_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID` (create the bot with @BotFather) and/or `AURORA_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL` (https; add its host to `config/network-policy.json`). With no channel, alerts only go to the journal.
+2. The daemon sends alerts through the governed egress proxy by default (`AURORA_ALERT_USE_EGRESS_PROXY=1`); `api.telegram.org` is already in the network policy.
+3. Install the external monitor (independent of the daemon, runs every minute and detects a dead service):
+
+```bash
+sudo cp deploy/aurora-monitor.service deploy/aurora-monitor.timer /etc/systemd/system/
+sudo systemctl daemon-reload
+sudo systemctl enable --now aurora-monitor.timer
+```
+
+The monitor sends directly (not through the egress proxy) so it still alerts if the proxy is down. Test it: `sudo systemctl stop aurora.service` and expect a message within ~2-3 minutes.
